---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
const title = "Website privacy";
const description = "How LLMSX website analytics, accounts, external links and local tools handle information, and where to send privacy requests.";
---
<Base title={title} description={description} route="/privacy/">
  <p>Publisher: Mitchell Hudson · Notice updated: 7 November 2026</p>
  <p>This notice covers the LLMSX website at llms-explorer.com and llmsx.org. The <a href="/net-dns-monitor/privacy/">Net-DNS-Monitor app has a separate privacy policy</a>. Other downloaded tools and model providers have their own data flows.</p>
  <h2>Reading public pages</h2>
  <p>You can read guides and download public reference files without creating an account. Requests still pass through the website's hosting infrastructure. The host receives the request URL, network address and ordinary browser request information needed to deliver the page.</p>
  <h2>Google Analytics</h2>
  <p>Public pages load Google Analytics to measure visits and interactions, such as navigation and guide or tool links. The custom handlers send bounded event names and public item identifiers for navigation, successful copies, failed copies and optional workflow outcome buttons. They do not send prompt text, copied content or search text. Custom event page URLs omit query strings and fragments. A reported outcome is the visitor’s self-report. Google may receive information such as the page URL and IP address and may use cookies. See <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">how Google uses information from partner sites</a> and the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout">Google Analytics browser opt-out</a>.</p>
  <p>The website skips its Analytics loader and custom events when the browser enables Do Not Track or Global Privacy Control, or the Google Analytics disable flag is set. Blocked analytics never prevents reading, downloading or copying.</p>
  <p>The website omits its Analytics and advertising loaders from sign-in, account, API-key, usage, contribution, donation, moderation, proposal and playground routes. That does not remove the network requests required for those features to work.</p>
  <h2>Advertising</h2>
  <p>Articles and curated concept references show ads served by Google AdSense. Other pages, including the home page, account routes and pages excluded from search, do not load the advertising script.</p>
  <p>Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on a visitor's prior visits to this website or other websites. Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads based on those visits. Google may receive the page URL, your network address and cookie identifiers. See <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">how Google uses information from partner sites</a> and <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads">how Google uses advertising cookies</a>.</p>
  <p>You can opt out of personalized advertising in Google's <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/">Ads Settings</a>. You can opt out of some third-party vendors' use of cookies for personalized advertising at <a href="https://optout.aboutads.info/">aboutads.info</a> or, in Europe, <a href="https://www.youronlinechoices.eu/">youronlinechoices.eu</a>. Visitors in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom and Switzerland are asked for consent through Google's consent message before personalized ads are shown.</p>
  <p>When the browser enables Global Privacy Control or Do Not Track, the website asks Google for non-personalized ads only. Non-personalized ads can still use cookies for frequency capping, fraud prevention and aggregate reporting. Blocking ads never prevents reading, downloading or copying.</p>
  <h2>Email updates</h2>
  <p>If you subscribe through the email-updates form, the site sends your email address to the LLMSX API. It stores the address, subscription and verification tokens, timestamps and subscription status. Confirmation and update emails are sent through the configured email service.</p>
  <p>The unsubscribe link stops further update notices. It marks the subscription as unsubscribed rather than deleting its stored record. Contact <a href="mailto:mitchphudson@gmail.com">mitchphudson@gmail.com</a> to request correction or deletion of subscription data.</p>
  <h2>Accounts and hosted features</h2>
  <p>If you sign in, the website sends authentication and account requests to the LLMSX API. Accounts use session cookies. The API stores account identity, authentication records, API-key records, usage and billing records. Inputs submitted to hosted features are sent to that service; reading a public article does not submit an input.</p>
  <p>For questions about your stored account data, retention, correction or deletion, contact <a href="mailto:mitchphudson@gmail.com">mitchphudson@gmail.com</a>. Do not place passwords, tokens or private account data in a public GitHub issue.</p>
  <h2>Downloads and external links</h2>
  <p>A downloaded tool can contact GitHub, a package registry or a model provider according to its configuration. Read the tool's requirements and settings before using it with private material. External links take you to services governed by their own privacy notices.</p>
  <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
  <p>This notice describes the current website implementation. It must be updated when that implementation changes. Send privacy questions to <a href="mailto:mitchphudson@gmail.com">mitchphudson@gmail.com</a>.</p>
</Base>
